Description: CVE-2026-50811: FT_Get_Var_Design_Coordinates() asked for more coordinates than a variable font has axes read the axis array of a TrueType GX or OpenType variable font past its end (TT_Get_Var_Design, ttgxvar.c; the same pattern in T1_Get_Var_Design of a Type 1 multiple master, t1load.c); the extra coordinates are now zeroed. CVE-2026-95512: a CID-keyed font whose subroutine dictionaries overlap made cid_read_subrs() allocate and decrypt the same data again for each of its font dictionaries (memory and CPU: a denial of service); their total is now limited to four times the size of the font. The fixes of 2.15.0 for crafted TrueType fonts found by Project Zero and OSS-Fuzz: the bytecode instruction SHZ moved the points of the whole glyph zone, phantom points and points past the last contour included, and with a zone of no contours took the whole twilight zone (a heap buffer overflow; work items 1419 and 1420); IUP and the interpolation of the deltas of a GX variation (tt_interpolate_deltas, tt_delta_interpolate) counted points and contours in signed counters that overflow on a glyph of more than 32767 points or contours (work items 1421 and 1423); FT_LOAD_COLOR rendered the COLRv0 layers of a glyph that is not an outline (a bitmap or SVG glyph) and loaded bitmap layers into it, reading past a bitmap of less than a byte per pixel (work item 1425): now only scalable COLRv0 layers are rendered. The fonts FreeType of az reads are the servers' own (ImageMagick, GD, fontconfig, OpenJDK); patched anyway (aZ, 12.11.2026), not the 2.15.0 take line
Origin: upstream FreeType https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/8fa928f1617aba65f45b00f0dcb109f077b7741e and https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/5a280ecde6f324de0d226261036e736e0cb49a71 (CVE-2026-50811, work item 1436, 13.05.2026), https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/f3ca71c9900fe860849b3163a6e2c1e765b291d9 (CVE-2026-95512, work item 1457, 07.09.2026), all three in 2.15.0, after 2.14.3; as Debian carries them on 2.14.3 (freetype 2.14.3+dfsg-3, debian/patches/CVE-2026-50811.patch and CVE-2026-95512.patch; Ubuntu 2.14.3+dfsg-2ubuntu1 and 2.14.2+dfsg-1ubuntu0.3 the same); the fixes of 2.15.0 as NixOS carries them on 2.14.3 (nixpkgs pkgs/by-name/fr/freetype/package.nix, master 31f93ff3, 12.11.2026): https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/1803559c4ee407d0bcbf2a67dbe96690cee869d2 and https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/7d600a022e1d813e85a8c94ffd395f6135872267 (SHZ, work items 1419, 1420, OSS-Fuzz 499455833 and 505900175), https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/7974be74d8b5a2fbf99aa88f0461d1f80af51cee (IUP, 1421), https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/0d45c7f1911bc6db0bf072eea0c8cdccd77bc6b3 (GX, 1423), https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/freetype/freetype/-/commit/cbe12767ea73d1006edc75fcd61c0b0d2a88f34e (FT_LOAD_COLOR, 1425), this one on the code of 2.14.3 as it is: NixOS takes the formatting commit 590b7701 before it, which only drops a switch with a lone default case and indents again; -p0

